## 4. Modular ownership

New module:

```text
runtime/bus/actionEventSubscriptionRegistry.mjs
```

Responsibilities:

```text
createActionEventSubscriptionRegistry()
subscribeActionEvents(registry, filterOrListener, listener)
publishActionEvent(registry, event, options = {})
getActionEventSubscriberCount(registry)
```

The registry owns:

```text
live listener registration
actionId / runId / type filtering
idempotent unsubscribe
normalized event publication through existing actionEvent validation
listener-error isolation
subscriber-list copying during publish
```

The registry does not retain events after publication.

---

## 5. Execution publication seam

`runtime.mjs` remains the composition root. It creates one event registry and injects a publisher into execute-action dispatch:

```text
createActionEventSubscriptionRegistry()
executeAction(...) -> runExecuteActionDispatch(..., { runNativeTextRequest, actionRequests, publishActionEvent })
subscribeActionEvents(...) -> bus-level subscription registry
```

`capabilityBusExecuteActionExecution.mjs` publishes existing outcome events only:

```text
startedOutcome.actionEvent
terminal outcome.actionEvent from completed / failed / cancelled / timeout mapping
```

Adapter/backend handle creation failures before `startedOutcome` creation do not publish a misleading started event in v1.

Publication errors are isolated from execute-action behavior. A subscriber/listener failure or publisher exception must not convert an otherwise valid action execution into a failed outcome.

