## 8. Real-runtime status

Real-runtime tests were run by Michael locally on Windows/MINGW64 from the candidate package.

Passed:

```bash
REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestExecuteActionCancellation.mjs
REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestExecuteActionPublicEnvelopeDispatch.mjs
REAL_RUNTIME=1 node ./tests/smokeTestNativeWorkerBackendExecutionIntegration.mjs
```

Observed successful real-runtime outcomes:

```text
[OK] REAL_RUNTIME cancelAction text.generate completed with cancelled outcome
[OK] REAL_RUNTIME executeAction raw action envelope text.generate completed
[OK] REAL_RUNTIME executeAction text.generate completed
```

Known non-blocking warnings appeared:

```text
ExperimentalWarning: Importing JSON modules is an experimental feature and might change at any time
[node-llama-cpp] load: control-looking token: 128247 '</s>' was not control-type; this is probably a bug in the model. its type will be overridden
```

Because this branch is parent-side/control-surface publication only and does not touch worker, scheduler, lifecycle, request settlement, or stream shaping internals, these existing real-runtime execute-action/cancel-action checks cover the native/model regression gate for the declared scope.

No additional real-runtime retest was required after merge because `main` was inspected for the declared branch scope and the local real-runtime checks passed on the uploaded candidate package.

